in-gap (val,q) with q<=149: [(3, 38), (4, 51), (5, 63), (5, 64), (6, 76), (6, 77), (7, 88), (7, 89), (7, 90), (8, 101), (8, 102), (8, 103), (9, 113), (9, 114)]
smallest q = 38  => gap needs q>=38, and q|pair-sum => 2*max(A)>=38 => max(A)>=19

PROVED: max(A)<=18 => M=1/13 or M>=2/25.

Can the DISCRETE necessary condition rule out each (val,q)? WLOG witness a=1 (lowest terms),
so R subset {val..q-val} in Z/q, and every k must have some c in R with |ck|_q <= val (else M>val/q).
=> min set-cover of Z/q by B_c={k:|ck|_q<=val}. If min cover > 12, that (val,q) is IMPOSSIBLE.

